  "question": "Let $p(x)$ be a continuous function which is positive for all $x$ and $\\int_2^3p(x)\\,dx=c\\int_0^2p\\left(\\frac{x+4}{2}\\right)\\,dx$. Then",
  "options": {
    "A": "$c=4$",
    "B": "$c=1/2$",
    "C": "$c=1/4$",
    "D": "$c=2$"
  },
  "answer": "B",
